  "originalQuery": "A Database Engineer is responsible for planning an upgrade of a Cloud Bigtable database to meet new performance requirements. The engineer must ensure that the upgrade results in a minimum performance improvement of 50% while maintaining data consistency and minimizing downtime. Which of the following strategies is the most appropriate to achieve these objectives?",
  "originalOptions": "A. Increase the number of Bigtable nodes in the existing cluster.<br/>B. Use Cloud Bigtable's managed backups to create a new instance with upgraded settings, and then switch the application to use the new instance.<br/>C. Export the data from the Bigtable instance, create a new instance with a more powerful machine type, import the data, and then switch the application to use the new instance.<br/>D. Implement horizontal partitioning in the existing Bigtable instance to distribute the data across multiple tables.",
  "domain": "Deploy scalable and highly available databases in Google Cloud",
  "hasImage": false,
